meta {
  name: 24 Outsource Sample
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/outsource
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "outsourceCenterId": "{{outsourceCenterId}}",
    "sendDate": "2026-10-08",
    "sendTime": "14:30",
    "logisticsType": "Courier",
    "outsourceStatus": "Dispatched",
    "notes": "Sent to third-party lab"
  }
}

tests {
  test("transition applied (or rejected by the state machine)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 404, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Outsource — **Accepted → Outsourced**, creating an OUTSOURCE `SampleTransfer`.

  `outsourceCenterId` is **optional at this step**: omit it to mark the sample
  Outsourced now and assign the center later via **Assign Center**
  (`POST /accession/transfers/:id/assign-center`) — mirroring the Internal Send
  flow whose station is likewise optional-then-assignable. When supplied it must
  reference an existing `OutsourceCenter` in the caller's tenant (validated → 404
  `ACCESSION_OUTSOURCE_CENTER_NOT_FOUND` if missing); when omitted the transfer is
  created with a null center.

  `sendDate`/`sendTime` are optional (the UI pre-fills them with "now"); `sendDate`
  defaults to the current time server-side when absent. Third-party labs don't use
  Kalnostic, so tracking is **manual** via `outsourceStatus` (CR-3). Bulk:
  `POST /accession/order-samples/bulk/outsource`.

  > To outsource *with* a center, set `{{outsourceCenterId}}` from the Outsource
  > Centers folder first; otherwise drop that body field to test the assign-later
  > flow.
}
